","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109012","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109012.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109012.patch","merged_at":"2025-09-22T13:56:28Z"},"body":"Fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100780\r\n\r\nIn majority of the cases this doesn't change anything, but if the gradient colors happen to be close you now get the full range without duplicates e.g.:\r\nMaster:\r\n<img width=\"515\" height=\"166\" alt=\"master_color\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/16442241-3a17-4497-8f3f-ff952f5642c4\" />\r\nThis pr:\r\n<img width=\"515\" height=\"166\" alt=\"pr_color\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7beb9f56-146b-4daf-9228-9e647a220b91\" />\r\n3px gradient from (11, 0, 11) to (13, 100, 13). The center pixel is now (12, 50, 12) instead of (11, 50, 11). (I know you can't see sh*t, but take a color picker and try yourself).\r\n\r\nRounding is necessary since color values are floats on disk and won't yield the same value when multiplied by 255.0 and floored:\r\nE.g. 11 is represented as `0.04313725`.\r\n```gdscript\r\nprint(String.num(0.04313725 * 255.0)) # 10.99999875\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/e